From e6759540117968f116f4b96145c0ddf8742e75b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: grenudi <idunerg@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 04:21:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: qcom: sm7150-lpass-lpi: fix the SoundWire data pin
 functions

Two SoundWire data pins have their function at the wrong mux index:

- gpio1 (TX data 1) selects swr_tx_data with mux 3, not 1;
- gpio5 (RX data 1) selects swr_rx_data with mux 2, not 3.

With the old table the TX bus reported a bus clash as soon as the WCD9375
codec enumerated, and the codec never finished its initialisation
("soundwire device init timeout"); with the mux indices corrected both
buses enumerate the codec and its registers can be read and written.

The indices are those of the vendor's device tree for this SoC (sm6150-lpi
in Xiaomi's GPL kernel for surya: tx_swr_data1 func3, rx_swr_data func2,
the pins counted from the start of the LPI block, 18 ahead of this
driver's numbering).

Tested on a Xiaomi POCO X3 NFC (surya).
---
 drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm7150-lpass-lpi.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm7150-lpass-lpi.c b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm7150-lpass-lpi.c
index 94b9b8725..a10338fe8 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm7150-lpass-lpi.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm7150-lpass-lpi.c
@@ -81,11 +81,11 @@ static const char * const swr_tx_data_groups[] = { "gpio1", "gpio2", "gpio5" };
 
 static const struct lpi_pingroup sm7150_groups[] = {
 	LPI_PINGROUP(0, 0, slimbus_clk, swr_tx_clk, _, _),
-	LPI_PINGROUP(1, 2, swr_tx_data, audio_ref, _, _),
+	LPI_PINGROUP(1, 2, _, audio_ref, swr_tx_data, _),
 	LPI_PINGROUP(2, 4, slimbus_data, swr_tx_data, _, _),
 	LPI_PINGROUP(3, 8, slimbus_data, swr_rx_clk, _, _),
 	LPI_PINGROUP(4, 10, slimbus_data, swr_rx_data, prim_mclk_a, _),
-	LPI_PINGROUP(5, 6, qua_mi2s_sclk, _, swr_rx_data, swr_tx_data),
+	LPI_PINGROUP(5, 6, qua_mi2s_sclk, swr_rx_data, _, swr_tx_data),
 	LPI_PINGROUP(6, LPI_NO_SLEW, qua_mi2s_ws, cdc_pdm_rx, _, _),
 	LPI_PINGROUP(7, LPI_NO_SLEW, qua_mi2s_data, _, _, _),
 	LPI_PINGROUP(8, LPI_NO_SLEW, qua_mi2s_data, dmic1_clk, _, _),
-- 
